{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And it shall be, when you come, etc., which HaShem swore to our fathers.</b> Therefore our Rabbis said that the convert brings [the first fruits] but does not recite [the declaration], for he cannot say 'to our fathers.' But in prayer he does say 'our Elohim and Elohim of our fathers,' for we rely on the Yerushalmi, which says that all converts are called by the name of Abraham — therefore he is called 'father of a multitude of nations.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:19.668428386Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}